,"type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The goods module has zero warnings, so any new ones would be ours to fix. I confirmed the detail page handles back navigation properly in the emulator. Now I'm drafting the acceptance.md file in chunks, writing the first part and planning to append the rest with proper IDs.\n\nI'm defining component IDs for the comment section, detail images, and image viewer elements, then structuring each acceptance item with fields for source, evidence level, atomic behavior, observable outcomes, entry conditions, preconditions, user actions, UI/data/network results, boundary conditions, and stability notes.\n\nGiven 37 items at roughly 13 lines each, I'm weighing whether to compress the eight dimensions into single-line summaries versus keeping them as readable sub-bullets, and considering merging closely related items (like count-marker rules, fullscreen behavior, and boundary cases) into their parent checkpoints to reduce redundancy while still preserving distinct testable behaviors.\n\nSettling on a final list of roughly 30 items, I'm drafting the numbered checkpoints: starting with Scene 1 covering entry into the detail page, data requests, the reviews section's position and visibility on scroll, nickname/star/text display, ordering, and fallback cases for missing nicknames or empty reviews. Then Scene 2 begins, covering thumbnail display rules — first image position, \"+1\" and \"+(N-1)\" count markers for multiple images, and handling single-image or no-image cases.\n\nContinuing into Scene 3, I'm outlining how the \"product details\" title appears after the review section, with detail images rendered in order, adaptive content sizing, loading backgrounds, scrollability to the end, and hiding the section entirely when there's no content. Scene 4 covers the full-screen image viewer triggered by tapping a thumbnail — showing the complete image list for that review, page indicators like \"1/2\", swipe navigation with page updates, closing via button or system back gesture, preserving scroll position on return, handling the \"+N\" marker tap, single-image viewer behavior, debouncing repeated taps, resetting state on reopen, and ensuring the viewer doesn't trigger any API calls or page reloads. Finally I'm adding cross-cutting concerns like request failure/retry behavior and what happens when returning to the detail page after navigating away and back.\n\nNow I'm planning to write the boundary matrix, state machine, unconfirmed items summary, selector summary, and copy text excerpts, starting with the header, conventions, and copy excerpts in the first chunk.\n\n","startTime":1792415835989,"lastModifiedTime":1792415853012},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_013Ew9kT23X99etJFyex1AaY","type":"TOOL","toolName":"write_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cm-spec26/spec/acceptance.md","content":{"$blob":"sha256:fe3e94e0bb28a0618dfbf62a8168b4181caffba6e99b5bd15b3e6303afe8ee2c","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":5646,"compression":"none"}},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Write file success","metadata":{"relativePath":"spec/acceptance.md","absolutePath":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cm-spec26/spec/acceptance.md","diff":{"add":52,"remove":0},"resolution":"absolute","originalContent":null,"content":{"$blob":"sha256:fe3e94e0bb28a0618dfbf62a8168b4181caffba6e99b5bd15b3e6303afe8ee2c","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":5646,"compression":"none"},"askReview":false,"runMode":"yolo"}},"accepted":true,"isRebuilt":false}]},{"id":"6ad6187ee2713b7e00fea669","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":19614},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"19afe916-876d-4550-bd5d-712f1d2e58b6","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Moving on to Section 3 now, working through scene 1 items in smaller chunks.\n\n","startTime":1792415875595,"lastModifiedTime":1792415875752},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01Afr8kXf5zxuJ27TazaHtMW","type":"TOOL","toolName":"edit_file","params":{"file_path":